<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Tórshavn</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Thorshavn</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Tórshavn is the capital and largest town of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/faroe-islands">Faroe Islands</a>, on the east coast of the island of Streymoy. Its name means <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thor">Thor</a>'s harbour. The assembly of the islands met on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tinganes">Tinganes</a> peninsula there from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/viking-age">Viking Age</a>, and the town later grew as the centre of the Danish trade monopoly. It is now the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/logting">Løgting</a> and the Faroese government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/torshavn.jpg" alt="Tórshavn" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: PanWoyteczek · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Is03002-Torshavn.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
